.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt CFLOW 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm cflow
.Nd print a C call graph
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl r
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility scans C source files and prints the direct call graph.
A root function is printed as
.Ar name : Ar line ;
direct callees are indented by four spaces and expanded recursively. A call back to a function
already on the current path is printed with a
.Dq (cycle)
marker. Only calls to functions defined in the input are shown.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl o Ar file
Write the graph to
.Ar file .
.Ar -
writes to standard output.
.It Fl r
Print the reverse graph: callers instead of callees.
.El
.Pp
Functions called by another function are printed nested, not again as a top-level root.
Functions with no callers are roots; after them, any remaining functions are printed so that a
call cycle is still visible.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for a file or output error, 2 for usage.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ctags 1 ,
.Xr cxref 1
.Sh STANDARDS
A documented subset of POSIX
.Nm cflow .
Preprocessor evaluation, function-pointer calls, calls to undefined functions and the
.Fl d ,
.Fl D ,
.Fl i ,
.Fl I ,
.Fl U
and
.Fl f
options are unsupported.
